TELUS Health is empowering every person to live their healthiest life. Guided by our vision, we are leveraging the power of our leading edge technology and focusing on the uniqueness of each individual to create the future of health. As a global-leading health and well-being provider – encompassing physical, mental and financial health – TELUS Health is improving health outcomes for consumers, patients, healthcare professionals, employers and employees.
-  
 Montreal 
 Permanent, Part-Time 
 In-Person 
 Our team and what we’ll accomplish together 
 At TELUS Health we’re committed to building the healthiest workplaces on the planet. That’s why we offer organizations a range of services that focus on mental, physical and financial health. Through our Workplace Support Programs (WSP) we support employers who wish to help employees facing specific challenges that may include mental health, behavioral or substance use issues. The programs provide professional assessment and counselling to support an individual's return to healthy productivity. These clinical interventions address issues requiring longer-term, more specialized or more intensive levels of care in order to prevent or manage workplace performance problems, absence and disability.
 What you’ll do 
 Reporting to the WSP team manager, you will be providing in-person and remote counselling services for TELUS Health Workplace Support Programs (WSP). Additionally, you will be providing mental health and substance use assessments, diagnosis, treatment recommendations and intervention.
 How you will make an impact:  
 You will provide counselling to adult clients that are eligible to TELUS Health Workplace Support Programs;
 You will manage the administrative requirements as dictated by TELUS Health’s clinical models.
 What you bring: 
 You have a Ph.D. or master's degree in Psychology;
 You have a minimum of five years post-graduate counselling experience;
 You are a member in good standing with the Quebec Order of Psychologists;
 You have prominent substance use and mental health assessment and diagnostic skills;
 You have the ability to adapt to clinical supervision;
 You have the ability to assess all types of psycho-social disorders and develop treatment plans;
 You have the ability to use or have knowledge of clinical assessment tools;
 You are Able to write clinical reports in a clear and concise manner;
 You have experience and expertise with mandated clients;
 You have basic knowledge of community resources and case management skills;
 You are proficient with Microsoft Office tools
 You have the ability to work in person / remotely and also collaborate in a team
 Why join TELUS Health? 
 A generous vacation policy to support work/life balance;  
 A flexible benefit plan that fits your individual and/or family needs, as of first day of employment;
 A 700$ well-being account and $5000 per year for mental health support;
 A fast-growing and dynamic organization that likes to promote from within;
 A pension plan with generous contribution from the employer to help you reach your retirement goals; 
 One volunteering day/year to support a cause that's important to you; 
 A work environment that supports diversity and inclusion;  
 Access to exclusive TELUS employee advantages and deals. 
 A bit about us 
